sn9.14:2.1 starts: “You sniff this water-born flower
sn9.14:2.2 starts: that hasn’t been given to you.
sn9.14:2.3 starts: This, dear sir, is a factor of stealing.
sn9.14:2.4 starts: You are a thief of a scent.”
sn10.4:4.1 starts: Whoever’s heart, all day, all night,
sn10.4:4.2 starts: delights in harmlessness
sn10.4:4.3 starts: with goodwill for all beings
sn10.4:4.4 starts: has no animosity with anyone at all.
sn7.17:2.1 starts: “What jobs are getting done,
sn7.17:2.2 starts: monk in the Sal forest?
sn7.17:2.3 starts: Alone in the wilderness,
sn7.17:2.4 starts: in what does Gotama
sn8.4:3.1 starts: Ven. Ānanda:
sn8.4:3.2 starts: your mind is on fire.
sn8.4:3.3 starts: Shun the theme of the beautiful
sn8.4:3.4 starts: accompanied by lust.
sn9.3:2.1 starts: “This monk strikes me as stupid:
sn9.3:2.2 starts: at the wrong time,
sn9.3:2.3 starts: roaming through the rugged mountains,
sn9.3:2.4 starts: undiscerning, unaware.
sn9.14:3.1 starts: The monk:
sn9.14:3.2 starts: I sniff at the lotus
sn9.14:3.3 starts: So why do you call me
sn9.14:3.4 starts: a thief of a scent?
sn9.14:4.1 starts: One who
sn9.14:4.2 starts: damages flowers,
sn9.14:4.3 starts: one of such ruthless behavior:
sn9.14:4.4 starts: why don’t you say it of him?”
sn9.14:5.1 starts: The devatā:
sn9.14:5.2 starts: smeared like a nursing diaper:
sn9.14:5.3 starts: to him
sn9.14:5.4 starts: It’s you
